Standards implemented: Ed25519 (RFC 8032) via WebCrypto; WebRTC data channels (RFC 8831), ICE (RFC 8445), STUN (RFC 8489), SDP fingerprints (RFC 8122), DEFLATE (RFC 1951), base64url (RFC 4648); SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4); Merkle transparency logs with
inclusion and consistency proofs (RFC 6962 / RFC 9162); RGA sequence CRDT (Roh et al., 2011); observed-remove sets
and last-writer-wins registers (Shapiro et al., 2011); the Mann–Whitney form of the ROC AUC.

The design lens the estate builds in — entropy-guided regulation (the Guided Entropy Principle), weighted
information pruning (WIPER), behavioural entropy signatures (BES — "GEP-Based Security: Behavioral Entropy Signatures for
Cybersecurity and DevOps", applied here by src/watch.mjs) and dual-map checking — is the work of
GARY W. FLOYD, Lumiea Systems Research Division (a subsidiary of ThunderStruck Service, LLC), New Caney, Texas.

This build draws directly on: Gary W. Floyd, Lumiea Systems Research Division — ThunderStruck Service, LLC —
"From GEP Stabilization to Dual-Map Ethical Reasoning," Derivation v0.2 (Open Defensive Prior Art, Creative
Commons). Its core result — a stable system can stabilise a wrong reference — is why a high-stakes call here must be
confirmed by an INDEPENDENT brain on another device (a copy of the same pattern agreeing proves nothing and is
refused), and why a call no brain can confirm is held for a human (PENDING) rather than forced either way.
It is also why a business's old decision rule, re-grown when the company is planted (src/plant.mjs), is checked
against what really happened and not only against the old rule: a faithful copy of a rule copies its mistakes too.

